Z||000015||Jimmy||10-02-2001||02:25 AM||||I'm bummed that I couldn't make it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Oh well, maybe next time?  <P>MinnGreenGT, LowFieroGT, Fierohoho, Tina, r u going on the fall cruise? I know KEV is.  I am going to try and make it.  <P>Just to let you guys know I had a mildly successfull night Friday.  I beat a C4 Vette, 2001 Stang GT, and lost to my buddy's rocket.  Tina someone asked me again about a really LOUD silver Fiero that has a V8!  I swear everybody knows about your car at the local hangouts!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BTW, KEV those headlights are working great.  Talked to some bikers that know a great place to get H4 bulbs at a cheap price.  Glad to see you get your car out to one of these UNSANCTIONED(lots of sarcasm) events!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Overall sounded like you guys and gals had a great time.<P>Jim||||reg||1
Z||000016||GodSend||10-02-2001||08:37 AM||||Minn,<P>They look good enough for me!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  I have two questions though.<P>1) Once you have cleaned out the inside, is there any going back? (ie - can you remove the coloured parts in one piece)<BR> <BR>2) I will get the coloured LEDS.  I was wondering how many, and what colors, do i need (abviously red  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||MinnGreenGT||10-02-2001||09:34 AM||||Jimmy- We're not sure yet about the cruise this weekend... depends on how much time we end up with.  We'd like to.  Did you get the H4 headlight conversion?  I've got it on mine- and love it!<P>GodSend-  If you look through the link posted above, there are pics of the taillight separated.  Yes, you can just as easily replace the colored insert as you can remove it.  As for bulbs, the Stop/Turn signals are Red 1157's (double filament), and the Turn signals are Amber 1156's (single filament).  You can use red for the turn signals if you want...doesn't really matter.  The backup lights are clear anyway- so no need to change.  It'll all make sense as soon as you separate the lens.<P>lowfierogt... got your pics, will post them soon.||||reg||1
